{
  "note": [
    "The Fork's fabric (DR-106), cut from the one Kalamontee layout in scripts/fabric-kalamontee.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. Like the Escalator it is in that file because of the pass it was cut in, not because it is near the Kalamontee station: it is the head of the Lawanda escalator (comptwo.zil 59-74).",
    "FORK.metadata.json v2: 8.8 x 3.6 x 6.4, the eye at the middle of the landing, built from props because both east corners are cut off on the diagonal. The game: \"This is a hallway which forks to the northeast and southeast. To the west is the top of a long escalator.\" (comptwo.zil 62-64). No object, door, sign or control: canon puts none here.",
    "West, the 2.8 x 2.8 escalator mouth with the landing plate carrying the floor through it and the comb plate just inside; through it the flight drops away at 30 degrees, and the soffit closes the view at about Lawanda x 16.8, so no part of Lawanda Platform is in this sightline. Northeast and southeast, a 2.2 x 2.6 mouth on each 2.263 m chamfer -- the mouth all but IS the corner, 3 cm of reveal either side -- each opening on a doorless corridor running 30 m to a dark bend: northeast the far end of the walk scripts/fabric-lawanda.mjs draws from Systems Corridor West's southwest mouth, southeast the way to Project Corridor West, which has no package yet. Between them the 3.2 m of east wall is the solid central pier.",
    "The floor is the head of the flight, 14.174 m over the Lawanda platform. FORK v2's largeObject starts the treads dropping at its own x -3.4 and has them 0.56 m under the floor at the wall; the accepted Lawanda flight puts its head tread level with this floor at the mouth plane, and that is how it is cut."
  ],
